{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537382-high-umbrood-and-reality","id":1537382,"title":"High Umbrood and Reality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-15T00:29:37-07:00","id":1537382,"title":"High Umbrood and Reality","content":"It's been said that the high umbra contains figures, concepts, and locations that have ever been thought or dreamed up by humans in the real world. But I have also heard some people argue that these concepts don't manifest in reality due to disbelief. And some of these beings, according to the Rules of Near Realms, seem to only have power in their own umbral bubble. For example, in the High Umbra there is a Star Wars universe or an Aliens vs Predator universe, for instance. A mage should be able to visit these universes and interact with them, theoretically, but would it be impossible for the mage to summon somethng from these universes (say, a Jedi, Xenomorph, a superhero, etc) into the real world as they would any other umbrood? If not, then how strong would these &quot;fictional&quot; high umbrood characters be? What might a strategy be for incorporating them into spirit mechanics?<br /> <br /> On a secondary note - what would it be like to visit these high umbra realms? A trip to the Star Wars universe sounds dynamic with a lot of potential, though I could see many ways for it to go wrong, too. Would spirit sphere work there as it would against spirits normally, or would other spheres need to be incorporated?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","user":"KingJohn","date":". 06-15-2024, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T13:45:36-07:00","id":1537523,"title":"","content":"I would say there is no star wars universe in the umbra or anithing as profound. There may be a concept of star wars as one spirit or a group of concepts for jedi blasters etc. But again they in my opinion would not have their own star wars &quot;reality&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T16:20:39-07:00","id":1537531,"title":"","content":"Space Opera in general has been around long enough to have reflections in the Umbra. I would think that Star Wars, Star Trek, and Doctor Who, have been around long enough with enough fans to start something. That said, figures like Robin Hood, King Arthur, Sinbad the Sailor, Rustam, and others have deeper roots and have had time to influence the Umbra. <br /> <br /> That said, Doctor Who and Star Trek have been on TV sets over much of the planet. Star Wars and Star Trek have had hit films. The sheer mass of impressions has to count. Granted Homer has had longer to influence the Umbra, but a popular TV show reaches a vast audience. It's assumed that more people saw the Shakespeare plays went they were broadcast in the 1970s and 80s than had seen them up to that point. That has to have an effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T20:26:45-07:00","id":1537542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537382-high-umbrood-and-reality?p=1537531#post1537531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted Homer has had longer to influence the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homer Simpson? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T00:24:26-07:00","id":1537547,"title":"","content":"There's no clearcut way to determine how you interact with such realms, though it isn't too hard to improvise, either.<br /> <br /> At first we're talking spirits here, and those spirits follow all the same rules as any other. They <b>can</b> definitely come out of their realms and be summoned with magic as absolutely any other spirit, and they use the same traits and charms.<br /> <br /> Umbral realms have their own rules, that can be more or less similar to the regular umbrascape or to the material. What's more important here is to define how the spheres work within and if there is such a thing as Paradox in the realm.<br /> <br /> More spiritual realms require conjunctional Spirit to work a lot of magics, or even let you manipulate objects and some creatures within with Spirit alone. More material realms let you work magic as in the material realm. And many realms may have additional, unique rules, with Astral Realms in particular frequently (specially closer to the Epiphanies) requiring conjunctional Mind.<br /> <br /> With that variation comes the variations on the nature of its denizens. Creatures within a realm aren't always spirits, they can be a number of other things:<br /> <br /> 1- They can be effectively material beings, if native to the realm. This can happen only to creatures that are perfect reflections of their material counterparts, like humans and normal animals without any special power or unnatural traits. If you bring such a creature to the material, there's nothing special about them;<br /> <br /> 2- They can be <b>Bygones</b>, supernatural entities rejected by the Consensus. They can be brought to the material world, but unless they're in a welcoming Reality Zone this will hurt a lot. Rules for Bygones can be found in God's &amp; Monsters, if you want you can adapt them so certain Bygones suffer Paradox or Unbelief instead of damage per turn, but in general they can't stay for long;<br /> <br /> 3- They can be stranger still. While not much explored and not necessarily the best approach, nothing says some of those entities can't be like some of the many supernatural beings that still reside unmolested in the world. Jedi may be effectively Awakened or Sorcerers, you may decide any of those aliens have their own rules and are effectively a new splat, and so on. I wouldn't thread such option lightly, but it's your game;<br /> <br /> Keep Adaptation in mind. The more an entity is adapted to an umbral environment impossible on Earth, the more likely they are to be Spirits, even if not originally so.<br /> <br /> Otherwise the form of such a Realm is up to you. There may be a realm for each great franchise, there may be a Space Opera realm where everyone exists at the same time, or anything in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T02:10:07-07:00","id":1537550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537382-high-umbrood-and-reality?p=1537542#post1537542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homer Simpson? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thirty years on an American TV hit is impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}